# Academic Research Assistant Platform

## What this is
An AI-powered workspace for academic researchers. Structured, guided AI assistance for reviewing papers, evaluating student submissions, and preparing work for publication. The platform's core value is AI assistance governed by a layered instruction system.

## Core domain model — use these terms exactly, never synonyms

| Term | Definition |
|------|-----------|
| Task | Primary unit of work. Container for documents, threads, memory, context. |
| Cluster | Optional grouping of related Tasks with shared KB and instructions. |
| Assignment | Cluster type specific to Student Paper Review. Groups all submissions for one assessment. |
| Submission | Task that is a child of an Assignment. Holds per-student data. |
| Thread | Focused AI conversation within a Task for a specific analytical activity. |
| Workflow | Sequential automated execution of thread types within a Task. |
| TaskMemory | Persistent structured findings accumulated across all threads in a Task. |
| InstructionLayer | Five-level hierarchy: platform → org → user → cluster → task/thread. |
| InstructionStudio | Platform area for authoring, versioning, and managing instructions. |
| ActivityLibrary | Predefined thread types per module with instructions, routing rules, execution specs. |
| AutomationExecutionSpec | Self-contained process definition for a thread type in automated workflow mode. |
| InterventionTrigger | Condition pausing an automated workflow. Four types only. |

## Modules
1. **External Paper Review** — review papers for publishers (MVP)
2. **Student Paper Review** — evaluate student submissions with Assignment/Submission hierarchy (MVP)
3. **Article Self-Review** — analyze own work before submission (Phase 1)

## Platform areas (not modules)
- **Dashboard** — daily starting point, task list, cluster views, workflow status
- **Instruction Studio** — author, version, test, and manage instructions (all five levels)
- **Admin Panel** — org admin user management, budget, storage

## Architecture principles
- API-first — all frontend interactions via REST API
- Every entity is an event — design for analytics from day one
- Instruction quality is product quality — master instructions are core IP
- No irreversible decisions in MVP
- RAG abstraction layer — document retrieval via service interface, not direct DB queries
- AI provider abstraction layer — routes through AWS Bedrock, never calls Anthropic SDK directly
- Structured logging everywhere — JSON, from day one
